{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit maximum and annual increase cap","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit of more than one and one-half times one month's rent. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current deposit.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; annual increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental units in New Jersey. Combined regular and pet security deposits may not exceed one and one-half times one month's rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month's rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline, itemization and double-damage penalty","requirement":"Within 30 days after a tenancy ends, a landlord must return the security deposit plus interest less deductions, and send an itemized list of any deductions by registered or certified mail.","key_value":"30 days","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"If the landlord fails to return the deposit or the tenant disputes deductions, the tenant may sue and the court may award double the amount wrongfully withheld plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit interest belongs to tenant","requirement":"Interest or earnings on a security deposit belong to the tenant and must be paid in cash or credited toward rent on the lease renewal or anniversary, or on January 31 if the tenant received written notice.","key_value":"annual interest paid on renewal/anniversary or January 31","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"The interest or earnings paid on the security deposit belongs to the tenant and shall be paid to the tenant in cash or credited toward rent due and owing on the ren ewal or anniversary of the tenant's lease or on January 31, if the tenant has been given written notice, that the interest payments will be paid on January 31 of each year (N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 (c)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Remedy for unpaid deposit interest or missing notice","requirement":"A landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the deposit account within 30 days and at each annual interest payment. If notice or interest is not provided, the tenant may apply the deposit plus 7% interest to rent.","key_value":"7% per annum","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1","quoted_span":"If a tenant does not receive proper notice or is not paid interest as required, the tenant may use the security deposit for payment of rent by giving the landlord written notice that the security money plus interest at the rate of 7% per annum be applied to rent payments or payments due or to become due  from the tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after displacement by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation","requirement":"Within five business days after a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation, or evacuation, the landlord must return the security deposit.","key_value":"5 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation in New Jersey when an official posts a no-occupancy notice or certifies displacement over seven days.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within five (5) business days after a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation, or evacuation, the landlord must return the security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after domestic violence lease termination","requirement":"When a tenant terminates a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available for return within 15 business days.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease under the Safe Housing Act due to domestic violence, where the leased premises are not controlled by a public housing authority or redevelopment agency.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease  is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant's security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant's agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
